    Save current configuration                      file_name=initial_configuration.xml
    Run Keyword And Ignore Error                    Get Active Aliases

Common Test Teardown
    [Documentation]  Cleans up testing environment after test case execution.
    ...              If test case execution fails or unallowed alarms are detected then logs will be collected.
    ...              IMPORTANT! Whenever "gNB" is mentioned here it also includes tested BTS with only LTE RAT configured on it (LTE only).
    ...
    ...              ARGS:
    ...              - force_logs_collection (bool): defines whether logs should be collected despite passing test case execution;
    ...                                              defaults to: False (logs collection will not be forced);
    ...                                              recommended value: False
    ...              - btslog (bool): defines whether btslog (syslog) should be collected from gNB after test case execution;
    ...                               defaults to: True (btslog from gNB will be collected);
    ...                               recommended value: True
    ...              - gnb_slave_btslog (bool): defines whether btslog (syslog) should be collected from slave part of Fullrack gNB after test case execution;
    ...                                         defaults to: False (btslog from slave gNB part will not be collected);
    ...                                         recommended value: True for Fullrack configuration, False otherwise
    ...              - stop_and_fix_gnb (bool): defines whether stop and fix mechnism should be executed for gNB;
    ...                                         if set to True and truckroll will be detected on gNB then test suite execution will be paused for manual investigation;
    ...                                         defaults to: False (stop and fix for gNB will never be triggered);
    ...                                         recommended value: True
    ...              - stop_and_fix_enb (bool): defines whether stop and fix mechnism should be executed for remote eNB;
    ...                                         if set to True and truckroll will be detected on remote eNB then test suite execution will be paused for manual investigation;
    ...                                         defaults to: False (stop and fix for remote eNB will never be triggered);
    ...                                         recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - sleeping_cell_test (bool): defines whether sleeping cell check should be performed;
    ...                                           defaults to: True (sleeping cell check will be performed);
    ...                                           recommended value: True
    ...              - report_tl_configuration (bool): defines whether testline configuration should be reported to Reporting Portal using SCF ID generated by Scout;
    ...                                                defaults to: True (testline configuration will be reported);
    ...                                                recommended value: True
    ...              - enb_btslog (bool): defines whether btslog (syslog) should be collected from remote eNB after test case execution;
    ...                                   defaults to: False (btslog from remote eNB will not be collected);
    ...                                   recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - recover_to_onair (bool): defines whether attempt to recover gNB to onAir state should be performed;
    ...                                         False is used mostly with test cases which operates in Test Dedicated State (TDS);
    ...                                         defaults to: True (recovery of gNB to onAir state will be attempted);
    ...                                         recommended value: False if test case should end with Test Dedicated State (TDS) active, True otherwise
    ...              - teardown_for_fault_10 (bool): defines whether attempt to recover gNB from active alarm with fault ID 10 should be performed;
    ...                                              probably deprecated and recover_to_onair should be used instead;
    ...                                              defaults to: False (recovery from fault 10 will not be attempted);
    ...                                              recommended value: False
    ...              - power_reset_bts (bool): defines whether power reset of gNB SMOD should be performed;
    ...                                        defaults to: False (gNB SMOD power reset will not be performed);
    ...                                        recommended value: False;
    ...              - lte_snapshot (bool): defines whether snapshot should be collected from remote eNB;
    ...                                     defaults to: False (snapshot from remote eNB will not be collected);
    ...                                     recommended value: True for NSA mode, False otherwise
    ...              - rmod_logs (bool): defines whether logs from gNB RMODs should be collected - either via LMI (if present) or via FHNET container;
    ...                                  defaults to: False (logs will not be collected from any gNB RMOD);
    ...                                  recommended value: True
    ...              - tcpdump_remote_file_path (str): absolute path on gNB SMOD for collected tcpdump file;
    ...                                                customized mostly when during test case execution there will be SMOD reset and /tmp isn't safe;
    ...                                                must have same value as tcpdump_remote_file_path from Common Test Setup;
    ...                                                defaults to: /tmp/test_setup_tcpdump.pcap (default tcpdump file storage path);
    ...                                                recommended value: /tmp/test_setup_tcpdump.pcap
